1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
 Here's a five-minute thing that will drastically improve the way that your manager sees you.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,680
 I once had an employee who would send me a two-sentence message every Friday.

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,660
 Here's my wins from the week. Here's my focus for next week.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,760
 Sometimes it would include a third thing, which is, here's what I need your help on.

5
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:16,600
 But they would do it every Friday, even though I never asked for that.

6
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:18,440
 And here's what happened as a result of that.

7
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:20,860
 Their updates were always fresh on my mind.

8
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:24,840
 So when I give my update to my boss, it was easy to always include their wins.

9
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:29,220
 That five-minute thing that they did every Friday created visibility not only to me,

10
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:31,320
 their direct manager, but all the way up.

11
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,240
 Second thing is it kept them aligned with things that matter.

12
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,880
 Because sometimes when they would say, this is my focus for next week,

13
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,700
 I would say, no, don't waste your time with that.

14
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,580
 Here's what I think you should be focusing on.

15
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:44,860
 Because what happens when employees aren't constantly communicating their work is there's drift.

16
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,940
 It's easy to spend two, three weeks working on something,

17
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:51,020
 and then you get done with it and realize, oh, nobody cared about that thing.

18
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,680
 I've said it before, and I'll say it again.

19
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,440
 Assume that nobody has a clue what you're working on.

20
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:56,800
 Don't assume that people see.

21
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,560
 Don't assume that people are paying attention.

22
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:01,400
 because nine times out of 10, they are not.

